96.24 349.25 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "3026ed93-ebc4-55ba-bd34-a65ece6c8914")) (text "INTER-SHEET INTERFACE (see wired power-flow overview)" (at 20.32 318.88 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left top)) (uuid "0501313e-5dfe-565e-a800-e617eb9feb1c")) (text "J2 + J3: two parallel 16-pin outputs, pin 1 = -12V. C34/C36 at J2, C59/C61 at J3 (22u each, replace the 100u cans).\nS9.0: +/-12V only; J2/J3 pins 11/12 (+5V) and CV/GATE (13-16) are open.\nD8 MAIN is the only status LED (rail LEDs removed): MAIN_LED_OK (U5 on, FLT/PGOOD valid) AND RUN. Any bad status after\nARMED or a U20 guard trip latches every rail off. P12_OK / N12_OK: logic + test pads.\nU20 overvoltage guard (S8.1): +12V > 14.88 V or -12V < -13.64 V nominal (corners 14.48-15.27 / 13.27-14.02 V) pulls OV_N\n-> FAULT -> U5 off. Own reference REF_OV = U21 TLV431B (R100, C67, TP17); U18/U20 LM2901B; R93, R94, R98, R99 are\n0.1 % / 25 ppm. The -12V channel compares MON_OVN with GND (no V3V3 term); D22 holds MON_OVN near -0.24 V (25 C only,\n<=0.15 mA) if V3V3 is lost while the rack holds -12V. S9.0: the former +5V comparators of U18/U20 are spares.\nS8.3: U18/U20 supplies are always-on VPD; outputs remain 3.3 V logic. No prototype qualification is claimed." (at 20.32 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c94a5d79-ec2c-535e-b165-6944f75398be")) (wire (pts (xy 25.4 339.09) (xy 40.64 339.09)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid "b5ff4b7b-c47a-5633-9ccc-3d7e04c74546")) (wire (pts (xy 25.4 349.25) (xy 40.64 349.25)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid "b0a5fc9a-6b4c-5bfc-ba26-577ab2d36c2a")) (wire (pts (xy 30.48 273.05) (xy 30.48 275.59)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid "46884213-9ee7-5887-b5f2-065547ab6717")) (wire (pts (xy 30.48 283.21) (xy 30.48 285.75)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid "0332117a-e26b-5a15-82cf-8b1917a32a16")) (wire (pts (xy 35.56 146.05) (xy 35.56 148.59)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid "